* ============================================================================
*  IRF7416  -  P-channel power MOSFET, SO-8             (cabinet R1, drawer A4)
* ============================================================================
*  Role in this circuit: the gate booster.  Its source sits on +12 V; when the
*  2N7002 pulls its gate down, Vgs becomes about -11 V and the device turns on
*  hard, delivering +12 V (through R4) to the IRFZ44N's gate.
*
*  Orientation matters: the SOURCE must be the +12 V terminal.  The body diode
*  of a P-channel device conducts drain -> source, so if the two terminals were
*  swapped the body diode would feed +12 V straight into the power MOSFET's gate
*  and the fan could never switch off.
*
*  Fit to the cabinet record:
*
*      Vgs(th)   -2.0 V typ                     -> vto = -2.0
*      Rds(on)   25 mOhm max at Vgs = -10 V     -> kp = 1 / (0.025 * 8) = 5.0
*      Vds max   30 V,  Id max 10 A, Pd 2.5 W
*
*  Level-1 model, ohmic region:
*
*      Vgs = -10 V ->  1/(5*8)     = 25 mOhm     (matches the spec)
*      Vgs = -11 V ->  1/(5*9)     = 22 mOhm
*      Vgs =  -1.5 V -> off
*
*  Vgs rating is +/-20 V; the booster node only ever swings between ~0 V and
*  +12 V, so Vgs stays inside -12 V .. 0 V.
*
*  Its input capacitance (Ciss = 1700 pF typical at Vds = -25 V, datasheet) is
*  drawn on the schematic as C2, and it is what makes R3 = 10 kOhm the slowest
*  part of the driver: 10 k * 1.7 n = 17 us.  At Klipper's default 100 Hz fan
*  PWM that is harmless; if you drive the fan at several kHz, drop R3 to 1 k
*  (tau = 1.7 us) and the 2N7002 still only has to sink 12 mA.
*
*  KiCad reads this file through Q3's "Sim.Library" / "Sim.Name" fields.
* ============================================================================
.model irf7416 pmos(level=1 vto=-2.0 kp=5.0)


* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*  Sub-circuit wrapper - why this exists
*
*  The schematic symbol numbers its pins the way the package's legs are
*  numbered, because KiCad connects symbol pin N to footprint pad N.  KiCad
*  then writes the SPICE line in symbol pin order, so the wrapper's .subckt
*  signature is written in that same package order and re-orders the terminals
*  here for ngspice (which wants MOSFET as D G S [B] and BJT as C B E).
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt mos_irf7416 S1 S2 S3 G D1 D2 D3 D4
M_int D1 G S1 S1 irf7416
*  S1 S2 S3 are the three source legs of the SO-8 and D1..D4 the four drain legs;
*  inside the package they are the same two nodes, so only one pair is needed for
*  the model.  The bulk (B) of a P-channel part is tied to its source.
.ends
